{
 "id": "Vectors-DotProduct-Definition",
 "title_en": "Definition and properties",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "k": "p",
   "t": {
    "en": "When we take the dot product of two vectors, the result is a scalar. For this reason, the dot product is also called the **scalar product**. Sometimes it is also called the **inner product**. The definition is as follows.",
    "sha": "a1f9843be42a",
    "zh": ""
   }
  },
  {
   "k": "box",
   "env": "definition",
   "title": {
    "en": "Dot product",
    "sha": "537d0274b5cf",
    "zh": ""
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "Let $\\vect{u}=\\left[\\begin{array}{c} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ u_n \\end{array}\\right]$, $\\vect{v}= \\left[\\begin{array}{c} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ v_n \\end{array}\\right]$ be two vectors in $\\R^n$. We define their **dot product** as",
      "sha": "9ddcdaae286a",
      "zh": ""
     }
    },
    {
     "k": "math",
     "tex": "\\vect{u}\\dotprod \\vect{v} = u_1v_1+u_2v_2+\\ldots+u_nv_n."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "box",
   "env": "example",
   "title": {
    "en": "Compute a dot product",
    "sha": "932e78d1ef17",
    "zh": ""
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "Find $\\vect{u} \\dotprod \\vect{v}$ for $\\vect{u}=\\mat{1,2,0,-1}^T$ and $\\vect{v}=\\mat{0,1,2,3}^T$.",
      "sha": "f8d1269c5c46",
      "zh": ""
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "solution",
   "title": null,
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "We have",
      "sha": "a2214cd5b1a4",
      "zh": ""
     }
    },
    {
     "k": "math",
     "tex": "\\begin{array}{rcl}\\vect{u} \\dotprod \\vect{v}\n    &=&\n        (1)(0) + (2)(1) + (0)(2) + (-1)(3) \\\\\n    &=&\n        0 + 2 + 0 + -3 \\\\\n    &=&\n        -1.\\end{array}"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "p",
   "t": {
    "en": "The dot product satisfies a number of important properties.",
    "sha": "add2a634b50b",
    "zh": ""
   }
  },
  {
   "k": "box",
   "env": "proposition",
   "title": {
    "en": "Properties of the dot product",
    "sha": "ef8d9892c9c5",
    "zh": ""
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "The dot product satisfies the following properties, where $\\vect{u},\\vect{v},\\vect{w}$ are vectors and $k,\\ell$ are scalars.",
      "sha": "7dd2df90cd69",
      "zh": ""
     }
    },
    {
     "k": "list",
     "ordered": false,
     "items": [
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "$\\vect{u}\\dotprod\\vect{v}=\\vect{v}\\dotprod\\vect{u}$.",
         "sha": "a6cff6dcc3e3",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "$\\vect{u}\\dotprod\\vect{u}\\geq 0$, and $\\vect{u}\\dotprod\\vect{u}=0$ if and only if $\\vect{u}=\\vect{0}$.",
         "sha": "cc64fa4d502e",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "$(k\\vect{u}+\\ell\\vect{v})\\dotprod\\vect{w}=k(\\vect{u}\\dotprod\\vect{w})+\\ell(\\vect{v}\\dotprod\\vect{w})$.",
         "sha": "e616e0c7a7e6",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "$\\vect{u}\\dotprod(k\\vect{v}+\\ell\\vect{w}) =k(\\vect{u}\\dotprod \\vect{v})+\\ell(\\vect{u}\\dotprod\\vect{w})$.",
         "sha": "8e6dd0947916",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "k": "p",
        "t": {
         "en": "$\\vect{u}\\dotprod\\vect{u}=\\norm{\\vect{u}}^2$.",
         "sha": "85892dbc5f20",
         "zh": ""
        }
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "p",
   "t": {
    "en": "The proof is left as an exercise. Note that, by the last part of the proposition, we can also use the dot product to find the length of a vector.",
    "sha": "f87f4a06ae59",
    "zh": ""
   }
  },
  {
   "k": "box",
   "env": "example",
   "title": {
    "en": "Length of a vector",
    "sha": "629c3fa7a7c3",
    "zh": ""
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "Use a dot product to find $\\norm{\\vect{u}}$, where",
      "sha": "be4ba9bfe53b",
      "zh": ""
     }
    },
    {
     "k": "math",
     "tex": "\\vect{u}\n    =\n    \\left[\\begin{array}{r}\n      2 \\\\\n      1 \\\\\n      4 \\\\\n      2\n    \\end{array}\\right]."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "solution",
   "title": null,
   "blocks": [
    {
     "k": "p",
     "t": {
      "en": "By the last part of Proposition “Properties of the dot product”, we have $\\norm{\\vect{u}} = \\sqrt {\\vect{u} \\dotprod \\vect{u}}$. We have $\\vect{u} \\dotprod \\vect{u} = 2^2+1^2+4^2+2^2 = 25$, and therefore $\\norm{\\vect{u}} = \\sqrt{\\vect{u} \\dotprod \\vect{u}} = \\sqrt{25} = 5$.",
      "sha": "eedc95984416",
      "zh": ""
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "exercises": [],
 "title_zh": "定义与性质"
}
